abstract: >-
  Metro-by-year panel (2013-2024, excluding 2020) and replication code in R and
  Python for a study of whether restrictive land-use regulation amplified the
  effects of employment shocks and remote-work exposure on renter cost burdens,
  rents and permitting across U.S. metropolitan areas. Includes source data from
  the American Community Survey, Building Permits Survey, QCEW, CPI and OMB
  delineations, metro averages of the Wharton and NZLUD regulation indexes,
  tables, figures and an interactive website.
